## Phase 4-5: Multi-Probe Chain Fusion
Status: COMPLETE
Date: 2026-06-09 (initial), 2026-06-10 (bug fixes, full correctness)
Source: lingo-db handleExecutionStepCPU() single-function pipeline pattern
Implementation:
  - ir_to_llvm.cpp: CompileMultiProbeChain() (~1100 lines, N-stage generalized)
  - duckdb_adapter.cpp: chain detection at outermost HJ (DFS-first), per-stage
    ProbeStageInfo collection (physical-plan-only, no IR), registration keyed
    by innermost eid
  - physical_hash_join.cpp: multi-probe dispatch at innermost HJ, passthrough
    at outer HJs (thread-local multi_probe_active_eid), chunk reinitialization
    to outer types, scratch-chunk first attempt before committing layout
  - physical_operator.cpp: CachingPhysicalOperator disables chunk caching for
    chain members (fused layout differs from member's own layout)
  - pipeline_executor.cpp: resets multi_probe_active_eid per executor
  - join_hashtable.cpp / aqp_jit.cpp: AQPJoinHTView population, writable
    output validity masks
  - aqp_jit.hpp / aqp_jit_abi.h: AQPMultiProbeState, chain registries
  - ir_to_llvm.h: ProbeStageInfo struct, CompileMultiProbeChain declaration
Description: Fuses consecutive HASH_JOIN probes on DuckDB probe pipeline into
  a single LLVM function. Eliminates per-operator dispatch overhead and enables
  cross-probe optimizations (shared hash values, register-resident intermediate
  values, no intermediate materialization). N-stage generalized codegen with
  per-stage skip_hash_cmp, payload pruning, and bail on overflow.

Bugs found and fixed (2026-06-09/10):
  1. Thread race on multi_probe_active_eid (was plain member, shared across
     pipeline worker threads) → static thread_local, reset per PipelineExecutor.
  2. Chain overwrite: DFS re-detected a shorter chain at a middle HJ of an
     N>=3 chain, overwriting the fused fn at the same innermost eid →
     already_in_chain check (multi_probe_fns / multi_probe_passthrough_eids)
     + skip single-probe registration for chain members.
  3. Build-side chains: fused output types broke the parent HJ's Sink →
     is_build_side flag threaded through RegisterJIT DFS, chain detection
     skipped on build pipelines.
  4. N>=3 passthrough type mismatch (23b crash): middle HJs verify input
     matches the CHAIN's outer types (not their own GetTypes()); fallback
     path restores the member's own layout if a previous passthrough left
     the chunk with the chain layout.
  5. Bail row loss after layout commit: post-commit bail restores this HJ's
     own output layout and falls through to the interpreter (which handles
     >2048-row outputs via HAVE_MORE_OUTPUT). HAVE_MORE_OUTPUT continuation
     also skips JIT dispatch entirely (state.scan_structure check) so a
     mid-scan interpreter pass is never clobbered.
  6. Perfect-join bypass (--single-column-int-join-mode, default ON):
     PhysicalHashJoin::Finalize forces the regular hash-table path for chain
     members (force_hash_join_for_chains + multi_probe_chain_members), since
     the fused probe reads JoinHashTable directly. Mirrors lingo-db, which
     has no perfect-HJ path. Dispatch still validates every chain member at
     runtime (count>0, !external, !perfect) and falls back gracefully.
  7. Sign-extension: non-i64 integer keys are sign-extended (not zero-
     extended) before hashing/comparison, matching DuckDB's key layout.
  8. NULL-validity (the last wrong-results bug — node-based 10c/29c, rc
     10c/22d/28a): fused codegen copied data slots blindly with no validity
     handling; NULL build columns (e.g. cast_info.person_role_id, NULL in
     1,435,424/1,435,439 filtered rows) emitted uninitialized garbage as
     "valid" MIN() inputs. Fix (both single-probe and multi-probe codegen):
       - Input validity: per-row bit check on probe chunk masks (branchless
         select-on-address against an all-valid i64 constant global).
       - HT row validity: AQPJoinHTView.has_row_validity (new ABI field at
         END of struct, offsets stable) + per-column bit in the row's
         validity byte prefix (TupleDataLayout convention).
       - NULL keys never match: key validity ANDed into the key-equality
         result (NULL key → linear probe terminates at an empty slot).
       - Output validity: dispatcher allocates fresh owned all-valid masks
         (MakeChunkViewAt writable_validity=true); JIT clears bits via RMW
         word stores for NULL outputs; NULL fixed-size values store zero;
         NULL varchar memcpy sources redirect to a 64-byte zero global.
       - Bail hazard: interpreter gather only CLEARS validity bits, so the
         single-probe bail path does chunk.Reset() to drop stale masks.
  9. CROSS_PRODUCT IR guard: ir_query_splitter skips SetJITPendingIR when
     the sub-query IR contains a CrossProductNode (IR is unusable for join
     matching; previously caused exceptions/garbage matching in RegisterJIT).

Correctness (2026-06-10, all 113 JOB queries, golden file comparison,
release build, both --jit-level=pipeline and pipeline + --jit-skip-hash-cmp):
  - none-split:            0 diffs, 0 crashes, 0 timeouts
  - node-based:            0 diffs, 0 crashes, 0 timeouts
  - relationship-center:   0 diffs, 0 crashes, 0 timeouts
  All previously-failing queries now pass, including the formerly
  "pre-existing" split-level failures (node-based 28b/28c, rc CROSS_PRODUCT
  set) — fixed by items 8 and 9 above.

### Corrected lingo-db execution model understanding (2026-06-09)

Lingo-db uses a HYBRID model — streaming within NestedMapOp regions (consecutive
hash-join probes share SSA values without materialization), but materialization
between ExecutionStepOp boundaries. For non-consecutive HJs (e.g., FILTER/PROJ
between them), lingo-db also materializes. Our consecutive-HJ fusion matches
lingo-db's streaming behavior within a single execution step.

